### 1. Register (valid)
POST http://localhost:3001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rana",
  "email": "rana222400@bue.edu.eg",
  "password": "123456",
  "role": "customer"
}

### 2. Register (same email again)
POST http://localhost:3001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rana",
  "email": "rana222400@bue.edu.eg",
  "password": "123456",
  "role": "customer"
}

### 3. Register (password too short)
POST http://localhost:3001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "123"
}

### 4. Register (role owner is not allowed)
POST http://localhost:3001/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test",
  "email": "owner@example.com",
  "password": "123456",
  "role": "owner"
}


### 5. Login (valid)
POST http://localhost:3001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "rana222400@bue.edu.eg",
  "password": "123456"
}

### 6. Login (wrong password)
POST http://localhost:3001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "rana222400@bue.edu.eg",
  "password": "wrongpass"
}

### 7. Login (email does not exist)
POST http://localhost:3001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "123456"
}

### 8. Login (to get token)
# @name login
POST http://localhost:3001/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "rana222400@bue.edu.eg",
  "password": "123456"
}

### 9. Me (no token) -> 401
GET http://localhost:3001/auth/me

### 10. Me (valid token) -> 200
GET http://localhost:3001/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 11. Me (tampered token) -> 401
GET http://localhost:3001/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}x

### 12. Owner-only as customer -> 403
GET http://localhost:3001/auth/owner-only
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}